OL,3,GNEWSA'Our son donating organs means he
OL,4,Ais still around'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe parents of a man from Surrey whose
OL,7,Fdonated organs went on to help nine
OL,8,Fpeople have said it "helped massively"
OL,9,Fas they navigated their grief.
OL,11,FGeorge Elliott, who was 23 when he died
OL,12,Fafter suffering an aneurysm in 2015,
OL,13,Fhad been interested in organ donation
OL,14,Fsince watching a television programme
OL,15,Faged 11.
OL,17,FHis parents Claire and Mark Elliott,
OL,18,Ffrom Oxted, believe his decision to
OL,19,Fdonate his organs means "he's still
OL,20,Faround".
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
